From 7469596184f42e9276a83107317d060380b71b8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:34:28 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] PCIe: qcom-ecam: Update power domain management and trace log

- Refactor power domain handling to use runtime PM on pdev->dev
directly instead of creating separate virtual devices, fixing
-EEXIST errors with SCMI genpds.
- Add 1000ms post-PERST# settle delay on re-initialization to allow
endpoints to complete reset sequences.
- Move sysfs_notify() outside raw_spinlock critical section
to prevent RT lockup when kernfs_notify() acquires sleeping locks.
- Check pci_host_initialized inside safety_lock to prevent MMIO access
to unmapped registers during concurrent deinit on SMP.
- Convert aer_inject spinlock to raw_spinlock to avoid "sleeping
function called from invalid context" errors on PREEMPT_RT.
- Move sysfs_remove_group() before teardown in remove path to prevent
UAF from concurrent sysfs writes.
- Enable runtime PM in probe with devm_pm_runtime_enable() for proper
cleanup on all exit paths.
- Fix documentation formatting and remove redundant delay between
deinit/init cycles.
- Add trace-based logging with severity levels
(ERROR/INFO/DEBUG) and a log_level sysfs attribute

Change-Id: I8006ad53201b2c822aa9b2a4823ec85af13a4694
Signed-off-by: Rama Krishna Phani A <ramkri@qti.qualcomm.com>
